# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 (slice S6, part 2) — serialized close + safe teardown
# Area: tab.
# Rationale: S2 records close states but never drives beforeunload/unload or
#   cleans up S3/S4/S5. Supply one pending close per tab, deterministic veto
#   replies, ClosePage/CloseContents sequencing, and deferred forced teardown.
# Last-Rebased: 2026-11-02 (Chromium 156.0.8078.74).
# Audit: verified DispatchBeforeUnload(bool), ClosePage(), CloseContents and
#   BeforeUnloadFired signatures at the pin. RenderFrameHostManager's
#   BeforeUnloadCompleted calls ClosePage itself when proceed_to_fire_unload is
#   true: return false there and post our explicit ClosePage exactly once.
#   S5's RunBeforeUnloadDialog synchronously returns false/stay; the veto posts
#   a cancelled completion, with no waiting dialog or orphaned close callback.
# Policy: concurrent ordinary/forced requests return busy, not duplicate replies.
#   Accepted close callbacks complete once, cancelled after veto or closed AFTER
#   tab.closed. Page CloseContents is a page-initiated tab close, distinct from
#   shell window.closed (which only hides/detaches tabs). Registry engine/force
#   teardown supersedes a pending request, preserving its callback/initiator.
#   Built-in content beforeunload/unload timeouts apply (BeforeUnloadTimeout
#   simulates proceed=true); a 30-second total deadline forces cleanup if no
#   completion arrives. Requested confirmations still veto immediately via S5.
# Lifetime: ID/generation-only posted tasks; no raw content/view/profile pointer
#   crosses queues. Finalizer runs after callbacks unwind, cancels S3 observer,
#   S5 favicon/media/security subscriptions and dialogs, invalidates leases with
#   reason tab_closed, clears delegate, destroys contents, emits one tab.closed
#   with shell/page/engine reason, then replies. No S3 observer duplicate event.
# Minimal frozen-file exceptions: planned delegate close/veto bodies forward;
#   registry RequestClose/DestroySession route into the controller and a private
#   friend-only removal seam reports actual destruction. Merely adding a cleanup
#   call to the old synchronous removal would delete an active observer callback.
#   attachment_lease.cc gains one closed-state rejection, preventing an invalidation
#   sink from reattaching a native child during close. No changes to S3/S5, app
#   lifecycle/frozen bridge BUILD.gn, or upstream C++ files. mac :core GN block.
#   Deferred destruction still requires callers to retain profiles and drain UI
#   tasks before profile teardown; startup/shutdown transport wiring is unchanged.
# Gate: build-p18 green attempt 1; G1-G5 PASS smoke-tab015.log, G3 grep -qa.
#   nm close-controller symbols and linked close-policy strings verified.
#   Full integrity: sequential newest-first reverse/forward temporary-index replay.
